===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|Straya|'Straya||informal}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂ews-|id=dawn}}
First attested 16th century, from {{uder|en|la|terra austrālis incōgnita||unknown southern land}}, from {{m|la|auster||the south wind}}. Used also in 1693 (quotation below). Popularised by {{w|Matthew Flinders}} in 1814 (quotation below).

Distantly cognate to {{m|en|Austria}}, containing the same Proto-Indo-European root, but through German where it retained the earlier sense of “east” rather than “south”.

See also [[Terra Australis]].

